package <%= basePackage %>.contract

import jakarta.enterprise.inject.Stereotype
import jakarta.inject.Singleton

/**
 * Marks a [<%= basePackage %>.kernel.Handler] implementation as one
 * the channel's container should discover and hand to the Mediator.
 *
 * The domain owns this annotation. Its meta-annotations are API-only
 * Jakarta standards that describe intent — "one container-managed
 * instance" — so the domain still names no framework, and neither API
 * reaches a runtime classpath (both are declared `compileOnly` /
 * `provided`).
 *
 * Each composition root interprets the marker in its own idiom:
 * Quarkus reads it as a CDI stereotype and Spring targets it with a
 * component-scan include filter. Micronaut's Kotlin bootstrap wires
 * handlers explicitly — its `@Import` escape hatch is Java-only — so
 * there the marker is documentation only.
 *
 * [Singleton] is a pseudo-scope: no client proxy, so a handler that
 * needs to dispatch must take a `Provider<Mediator>` rather than a
 * `Mediator` — see the project's AGENTS.md §2. It is also what keeps
 * Kotlin's final-by-default classes usable as beans without the
 * all-open compiler plugin.
 */
@Stereotype
@Singleton
@MustBeDocumented
@Retention(AnnotationRetention.RUNTIME)
@Target(AnnotationTarget.CLASS)
annotation class DomainHandler
